  "body": "User decision (2026-11-07): \"No patch cuts at all is the way to go, do not spend time or tokens on those. Make sure they are tested but do that as a subtask that we are not waiting for.\"\n\n- Issue Law: a fix/perf/refactor PR merges once its independent review is clean and its quick gate green - no cut; feat/breaking PRs merge at the minor/major cut; the in-review comment says \"merges when reviewed\".\n- Commits and Releases: the PATCH row becomes \"no cut - ships in the next minor\"; \"When to cut\" is MAJOR/MINOR only; new \"Fixes are tested in the background\": after a fix merges, a gate-runner runs the batch tier on main in its own worktree and nothing waits for it - a red result becomes a new issue.\n- The publish paragraph drops the patch-tag wording.\n\n(The 0.12.2 cut in progress was stopped and its unpushed release branch dropped; #84's fix is on main and ships in the next minor.)\n\nChangelog: none (docs/process only)",
